*** ch14-04-variant-vending-machine — ACU vending machine with variant change equation: variants, irreducibility, variant unify (plain/filtered/constrained), variant match (Maude manual §14.4, §14.5, §14.9, §14.10, §14.13)

mod VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE is
 sorts Coin Item Marking Money State .
 subsort Coin < Money .
 op empty : -> Money .
 op __ : Money Money -> Money [assoc comm id: empty] .
 subsort Money Item < Marking .
 op __ : Marking Marking -> Marking [assoc comm id: empty] .
 op <_> : Marking -> State .
 ops $ q : -> Coin .
 ops a c : -> Item .
 var M : Marking .
 rl [buy-c] : < M $ > => < M c > .
 rl [buy-a] : < M $ > => < M a q > .
 eq [change] : q q q q M = $ M [variant] .
endm

*** §14.4: 4 irredundant variants of the __ symbol (FVP check)
get irredundant variants in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       X:Marking Y:Marking .

*** §14.4: 2 irredundant variants of the state < $ q q X:Marking >
get irredundant variants in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < $ q q X:Marking > .

*** §14.5: irreducibility constraints leave only Variant 1
get irredundant variants in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < $ q q X:Marking >
       such that q q X:Marking, q X:Marking, X:Marking irreducible .

*** §14.9: 2 variant unifiers (not minimal)
variant unify in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < q q X:Marking > =? < $ Y:Marking >  .

*** §14.9: filtered version returns the single most general unifier
filtered variant unify in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < q q X:Marking > =? < $ Y:Marking >  .

*** §14.10: irreducibility constraints discard the q q %1:Marking unifier
variant unify in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < q q X:Marking > =? < $ Y:Marking >
       such that q q X:Marking, q X:Marking, X:Marking irreducible .

*** §14.13: variant match — righthand side treated as ground
variant match in VARIANT-VENDING-MACHINE :
       < q q X:Marking > <=? < $ Y:Marking >  .
